--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Configuration directive documentation
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

src/directiveRegistry.ts and src/registry/ describe the props.conf and transforms.conf
attributes this engine recognises. Those descriptions are written for this
project. Where they restate what an attribute does, they describe documented,
observable behaviour of the software; they are not copied from Splunk's
documentation or from the .spec files that ship with Splunk Enterprise, and
those files are not reproduced here.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
PCRE2
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

The engine runs pcre2.wasm, and its consumers ship it. It is PCRE2 compiled to
WebAssembly. It comes from the pcre2-wasm-utf16 package, a dependency of this
project maintained in its own repository:

    https://github.com/Bimmiest/pcre2-wasm-utf16

The module is:

    PCRE2 - Perl-Compatible Regular Expressions
    https://github.com/PCRE2Project/pcre2
    Copyright (c) 1997-2007 University of Cambridge
    Copyright (c) 2007-2024 Philip Hazel
    SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause WITH PCRE2-exception

PCRE2's licence is reproduced in full in that package's LICENCE-PCRE2.md, and
its NOTICE describes what the package contains; both are installed with it
(node_modules/pcre2-wasm-utf16/). The PCRE2 source is not vendored in either
repository; the package's build script downloads the pinned release and
verifies its checksum.
